   "id": "avodah_zarah.40b.5",
   "daf": "40b",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "וְזֵיתֵי גְלוּסְקָאוֹת הַמְגוּלְגָּלִין. פְּשִׁיטָא! לֹא נִצְרְכָא אַף עַל גַּב דְּרָפֵי טוּבָא. מַהוּ דְּתֵימָא: חַמְרָא רְמָא בְּהוּ, קָא מַשְׁמַע לַן: הָנֵי מֵחֲמַת מִישְׁחָא הוּא דִּרְפוּ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «And rolled olive cakes.» The Gemara asks: Isn’t it «obvious» that these are permitted? For what reason might they be prohibited? The Gemara answers: «No, it is necessary» to teach that they are permitted «even though they are very soft. Lest you say» that there is a concern that they softened because a gentile «placed wine in them,» the mishna therefore «teaches us» that «these» olives «have softened due to the oil» they possess."
  }
